            "description": "Uploads a Kerberos keytab file for Site Web Proxy and returns an encrypted payload.\nThis operation is a pre-step for configuring Kerberos authentication in siteWebProxy policy.\n\nThe request must be sent as a GraphQL multipart/form-data upload\n(graphql-multipart-request-spec): `input.file` is `null` in `operations`, and the\nfile bytes are sent as a separate form-data part mapped to it via `map`.\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \"https://api.catonetworks.com/api/v1/graphql2\" \\\n  -H \"x-api-key: <API_KEY>\" \\\n  -F 'operations={\"query\":\"mutation encryptKeytabFile($accountId: ID!, $input: EncryptKeytabFileInput!) { webProxyConfig(accountId: $accountId) { encryptKeytabFile(input: $input) { encryptedFile } } }\",\"variables\":{\"accountId\":\"123\",\"input\":{\"file\":null}}}' \\\n  -F 'map={\"0\":[\"variables.input.file\"]}' \\\n  -F '0=@/path/to/file.keytab'\n```",
